ANS 3-
The Orders table is the fact table, while Customers, Restaurants, and DateTable are dimension tables.
Create one-to-many relationships from each dimension to Orders, this reduces duplication and simplifies DAX calculations.

ANS 4-
A calculated column computes and stores a value for each row,
while a measure calculates results dynamically based on filter context.
Use Total Revenue = SUM(Orders[Revenue]) for the KPI card so it responds to the City slicer.

ANS 5-
Two possible causes are a DAX measure using ALL() or REMOVEFILTERS(), or a disabled visual interaction/incorrect relationship.
Check the measure, Edit interactions, and Model view to identify the cause.

ANS 6-
In Modeling → Manage roles, create roles with filters such as [City] = "Ahmedabad" and [City] = "Surat".
Test using View as, publish the report, then assign users to their respective roles under Power BI Service → Semantic model → Security.
